package com.linguapro.android

object ScenarioBankC1 {
    private fun s(n: Int, text: String, a: ScenarioQuestion, b: ScenarioQuestion, transfer: String, c: ScenarioQuestion) =
        UnitScenario("C1-U$n", text, a, b, transfer, c)
    val items = listOf(
        s(1, "The pilot produced encouraging results, and the project team was understandably eager to secure further funding. Nevertheless, the participants had volunteered, the comparison period was short, and no equivalent group had followed the previous procedure at the same time. The reviewer recommended continuing the work while revising the claim that the pilot demonstrated effectiveness. This was not a dismissal of the observed improvement. It was a distinction between evidence that justifies further investigation and evidence strong enough to support a general causal conclusion. The revised report retained the positive result but made its inferential limits visible.",
            sq("What distinction does the reviewer insist on?", "Promising observations versus a general causal conclusion", "Positive observations versus an absence of any result", "Funding requests versus all scientific work as invalid", "İyileşme reddedilmiyor; genellenebilir nedensel sonuç için kanıtın sınırlılığı vurgulanıyor."),
            sq("How does the revised report handle the positive result?", "It retains it while qualifying the inference.", "It removes every positive observation.", "It presents it as definitive proof.", "Retained positive result ile inferential limits birlikte korunur."),
            "The programme improved outcomes in a small uncontrolled pilot. The authors call the result a reason for further testing.",
            sq("Which conclusion is proportional to the evidence?", "The result motivates further study.", "Universal effectiveness has been proven.", "No improvement was observed.", "Uncontrolled pilot, gözlenen sonucu genel etkililik kanıtı yapmaz.")),
        s(2, "The original email read, We need this fixed today. That wording expressed urgency but left responsibility and scope unclear. In revising it for a senior external partner, the writer specified the fault, explained its effect on the shared timetable, and asked whether a correction could be confirmed by the afternoon. She resisted replacing every direct phrase with elaborate ceremony: excessive formality would have made the practical request harder to identify. The final message was respectful and precise. Its register changed without obscuring what action was needed, who could provide it, or why the timing mattered.",
            sq("What principle guides the revision?", "Respectful register should preserve practical clarity.", "Formality requires removing all deadlines.", "Urgency can only be conveyed rudely.", "Respectful and precise, üslup ile açık eylem bilgisini birlikte tutar."),
            sq("Why does the writer avoid excessive ceremony?", "It could conceal the practical request.", "It would make the fault disappear.", "It would automatically guarantee compliance.", "Harder to identify, aşırı resmiyetin eylemi belirsizleştirme riskidir."),
            "The revised request is more courteous, but still names the required action and deadline.",
            sq("What has been preserved despite the register change?", "Operational clarity", "The original ambiguity", "An absence of responsibility", "Action ve deadline korunarak pratik açıklık sürer.")),
        s(3, "Two reports appear to disagree about a training programme. The first records satisfaction immediately after the sessions; the second examines whether participants use the skills six months later. A careless synthesis might describe one report as positive and the other as negative, as though they answered the same question. A more useful synthesis identifies the different outcomes and time frames, then asks how they relate. Participants can appreciate a course without consistently transferring its content into practice. The reports therefore need not cancel each other out. Together, they suggest that immediate approval and sustained application require separate evaluation.",
            sq("Why might the reports' conclusions coexist?", "They measure different outcomes at different times.", "They use exactly the same outcome and date.", "Neither report contains any evidence.", "Satisfaction ile sustained application ve hemen/altı ay sonra ölçümleri farklıdır."),
            sq("What would the careless synthesis overlook?", "The difference between approval and transfer into practice", "The existence of a course title only", "A proven absence of satisfaction", "Olumlu/olumsuz ikiliği, iki farklı araştırma sorusunu aynıymış gibi sunar."),
            "One survey measures enjoyment, another measures later use. Their different scores are not automatically contradictory.",
            sq("What should a synthesis first identify?", "What each measure actually evaluates", "Which score sounds more dramatic", "A reason to discard both without reading", "Önce ölçülen sonuçların ayrılığı saptanmalıdır.")),
        s(4, "The proposal's strongest argument was that a common platform could reduce duplicated work. Its weakest paragraph implied that opponents were merely protecting their departments. At a review meeting, the author was asked to address the practical objection instead: some teams needed specialist functions that the common platform did not yet provide. Removing the speculation about motives did not weaken the case for coordination. It required the case to explain how genuine differences would be accommodated. The revision proposed a shared core with limited specialist modules and acknowledged the additional maintenance this would entail. The argument became more persuasive by taking a counterargument seriously rather than dismissing its advocates.",
            sq("What strengthens the revised argument?", "Addressing the practical objection instead of speculating about motives", "Describing all opponents as selfish", "Denying any specialist requirements", "Motif yargısı yerine işlev ihtiyacına cevap verilmesi argümanı güçlendirir."),
            sq("What cost does the revision acknowledge?", "Additional maintenance for specialist modules", "The total disappearance of coordination", "No maintenance of any kind", "Would entail additional maintenance, çözümün bedelini saklamaz."),
            "Critics need a specialist function. Answering that need is more relevant than calling them resistant.",
            sq("What changes in the argument's focus?", "From presumed motives to the substantive objection", "From evidence to personal accusation", "From requirements to ignoring all criticism", "Gereksinim doğrudan ele alınır; niyet varsayımı geri çekilir.")),
        s(5, "The negotiators had publicly committed to different deadlines, making an immediate concession difficult for either side. The mediator asked what each deadline was intended to protect. One protected a public announcement; the other protected enough time for quality checks. Once these interests were separated from the stated dates, a staged arrangement became possible: a limited announcement could precede full implementation, provided the announcement accurately described the unfinished work. Neither side received its original demand unchanged. Both could, however, explain the agreement in terms of the interest it protected. The solution depended as much on honest communication as on the revised timetable.",
            sq("What made the staged agreement possible?", "Separating underlying interests from stated positions", "Giving both original demands unchanged", "Concealing all unfinished work", "Tarihler arkasındaki amaçlar ayrılınca duyuru ve uygulama aşamalandırılabildi."),
            sq("What condition protects the integrity of the announcement?", "It must accurately describe unfinished work.", "It must claim implementation is complete.", "It must contain no information about progress.", "Provided ... accurately described, duyurunun doğru kapsamla yapılması koşuludur."),
            "One side needs visibility; the other needs testing time. A limited demonstration can serve both if its limits are stated.",
            sq("What is essential to this compromise?", "Transparent limits on the demonstration", "A false claim of complete delivery", "Ignoring either side's interest", "If its limits are stated, uzlaşmayı dürüst sunuma bağlar.")),
        s(6, "A widely circulated article presented a striking conclusion, but its supporting citation referred to a commentary rather than to the original study. When the student traced the reference, she found that the study's authors had used narrower language and had discussed several limitations. She did not assume that circulation made the article worthless, nor that a citation made its interpretation reliable. Instead, she distinguished the original finding, the commentary's interpretation, and the later article's stronger claim. Her essay cited the original evidence for what it actually established and used the commentary only when discussing how the finding had been interpreted.",
            sq("What does tracing the reference reveal?", "The later claim was stronger than the original finding.", "All cited material was identical in wording.", "The original study did not exist.", "Narrower language, kaynak ile sonradan güçlenen yorum arasındaki farkı gösterir."),
            sq("How is the commentary used in the essay?", "As evidence of interpretation, not as the original finding", "As automatic proof of the strongest claim", "As a substitute for every source distinction", "Commentary, bulgunun nasıl yorumlandığını tartışmak için kullanılır."),
            "The review cites an editorial, but the underlying study states a narrower result.",
            sq("What should the writer do before repeating the claim?", "Check and distinguish the original result from commentary", "Treat citation alone as proof of accuracy", "Ignore the study because an editorial exists", "Atıf zincirindeki yorum ile özgün sonuç ayrılmalıdır.")),
        s(7, "The consultation document invited public responses, yet most questions asked residents to choose between two versions of the same policy. A community group argued that this excluded the option they cared about most. The council replied that the broader decision had already been made, while implementation remained open. The dispute therefore concerned not only preferred outcomes but the meaning of consultation itself. A revised introduction stated which decisions were settled, which could still change, and how responses would be used. This did not guarantee agreement, but reduced the risk that participation would be presented as influence over choices no longer available.",
            sq("What ambiguity lies at the centre of the dispute?", "Which decisions public responses can still influence", "Whether residents can read any questions", "Whether implementation has a name", "Consultation kapsamı, açık ve kapanmış kararların ayrılığıyla ilgilidir."),
            sq("What does the revised introduction clarify?", "Settled choices, open choices and the use of responses", "That every decision can be reversed automatically", "That no response will be considered", "Üç alanı açıklar; uzlaşma garantisi vermez."),
            "The location is fixed, but residents can influence access arrangements. The notice now states this explicitly.",
            sq("What misleading impression is reduced?", "That residents can still change the location", "That access arrangements are open", "That a notice exists", "Fixed location ile open access kararlarının sınırı belirginleşir.")),
        s(8, "The draft's opening sentence announced that a comprehensive, integrated and multifaceted review had been undertaken. It took another paragraph to say what had actually been reviewed. An editor moved the concrete action to the front and removed modifiers that added little information. She retained a qualification about the review's limited period because that changed how readers should interpret the finding. Concision was therefore not achieved by deleting every caveat or shortening every sentence equally. It came from distinguishing information that carried meaning from language that merely sounded substantial. The revised opening was shorter, yet more precise about both the work and its limits.",
            sq("What principle distinguishes good concision from mere shortening?", "Retaining qualifications that affect meaning", "Deleting every caveat", "Keeping abstract modifiers at any cost", "Limited period yorumu etkilediği için korunuyor; içi boş sıfatlar çıkarılıyor."),
            sq("What was moved to the opening?", "The concrete action reviewed", "An unrelated decorative phrase", "Every supporting table", "What actually reviewed somut bilgi olarak öne alınır."),
            "The editor removed repeated adjectives but kept the sample limitation.",
            sq("Why was the limitation retained?", "It changes the interpretation of the result.", "It merely makes the sentence longer.", "It proves the result applies everywhere.", "Anlamı belirleyen sınırlılık, gereksiz tekrar değildir.")),
        s(9, "An internal note described a delay as technically manageable. For the engineering team, this meant that a workaround existed. For the customer team, the same phrase suggested that the promised service would be unaffected. The communications lead rewrote the update for each audience, keeping the underlying facts consistent: the workaround preserved part of the service, but users would still face a temporary restriction. Audience adaptation did not justify changing the facts. It required selecting the implications each group needed to act on, while ensuring that no version turned a partial mitigation into a claim that the problem had disappeared.",
            sq("What must remain consistent across audience-specific updates?", "The underlying facts", "Every technical term regardless of usefulness", "The assumption that restrictions do not exist", "Uyarlanan vurgu olsa da partial mitigation ve restriction gerçekleri korunmalıdır."),
            sq("What did the phrase 'technically manageable' risk concealing?", "A remaining user restriction", "The existence of any workaround", "The engineering team's name", "Mühendislik çözümü, kullanıcıya etkisizlik anlamına gelmiyor."),
            "The workaround preserves basic access but not every feature. Both audience versions must state that limit.",
            sq("Which statement would distort the facts?", "The service is entirely unaffected.", "Basic access is preserved.", "Some features remain unavailable.", "Entirely unaffected, kısmi çözümü tam çözüm gibi sunar.")),
        s(10, "The decision had to be made before reliable long-term data would be available. One adviser argued that uncertainty justified waiting indefinitely; another argued that urgency justified ignoring it. The chair rejected that binary choice. A reversible step could address the immediate problem while reserving a larger commitment for later evidence. The minutes recorded the assumptions, the potential harms, and the conditions under which the decision would be revisited. Uncertainty was neither eliminated nor treated as a universal excuse for inaction. It became part of the decision's design, including how the organisation would recognise that its provisional judgement needed to change.",
            sq("What alternative does the chair offer?", "A reversible step with explicit review conditions", "Indefinite waiting as the only option", "Ignoring uncertainty entirely", "Reversible step, hemen eylem ile sonraki kanıtı birlikte düzenler."),
            sq("How is uncertainty incorporated?", "Through recorded assumptions and conditions for revision", "By claiming it has disappeared", "By forbidding later review", "Varsayımlar ve yeniden değerlendirme koşulları karara dahil edilir."),
            "We will take a reversible step now and review it if the assumptions fail.",
            sq("What characterises the decision?", "Provisional action with a trigger for reconsideration", "An irreversible claim of certainty", "A commitment never to act", "If assumptions fail, kararın yeniden ele alınma eşiğidir.")),
        s(11, "Three sources gave different accounts of a service reform. The administrative report measured processing time, an interview study explored staff experience, and a user survey examined access. None offered a complete evaluation by itself. The reviewer resisted combining them into a single undifferentiated score. Instead, she asked which dimensions converged and where improvement for one group might coexist with a cost for another. Faster processing appeared compatible with increased pressure on staff, while some users still found access difficult. The synthesis preserved this tension and recommended further investigation of the uneven effects rather than announcing that the reform was simply a success or a failure.",
            sq("Why is a single score potentially inadequate?", "The sources address different dimensions and groups.", "Every source measures the same thing identically.", "No source contains any relevant information.", "Hız, personel deneyimi ve erişim farklı boyutlardır; tek puan gerilimi gizleyebilir."),
            sq("What conclusion does the synthesis preserve?", "Improvement and costs can coexist unevenly.", "Faster processing proves universal benefit.", "One user's difficulty disproves every improvement.", "Increased pressure ve faster processing birlikte gerçekleşebilir."),
            "The service is faster overall, but some users face greater access difficulty.",
            sq("Which synthesis is faithful?", "Efficiency gains coexist with uneven access effects.", "Every user benefits equally.", "There has been no efficiency gain.", "Overall ve some users farklı dağılımları belirtir.")),
        s(12, "The executive summary originally repeated the report's background and left the requested decision until the final page. Directors understood the history but remained unclear about what approval would authorise. The writer reorganised it around the choice, the supporting evidence, the principal risk, and the consequence of postponement. Detailed assumptions remained in the annex, with a reference where they affected the recommendation. The revision did not remove complexity by pretending the decision was risk-free. It made the complexity usable: readers could identify the proposed commitment, see what it depended on, and decide which uncertainty required attention before approval.",
            sq("What did the original summary fail to clarify?", "What approval would authorise", "Every historical detail", "Whether a report had been written", "Background vardı, fakat istenen kararın kapsamı açık değildi."),
            sq("How is complexity made usable in the revision?", "By organising it around the decision and its dependencies", "By describing the decision as risk-free", "By deleting all assumptions without reference", "Choice, evidence, risk ve postponement sonucu karar yapısını oluşturur."),
            "The summary names the proposed commitment and the assumption on which it depends.",
            sq("What can the reader now assess?", "The decision and a relevant uncertainty", "A guarantee that no uncertainty exists", "Only the report's length", "Commitment ve depends on, karar ile dayandığı varsayımı birlikte görünür kılar.")),
        s(13, "The manager said the team had moved the goalposts, but the conversation revealed two competing interpretations. The customer regarded a newly requested feature as part of the original promise; the team regarded it as an expansion. Using the idiom expressed frustration but did not resolve the disagreement about scope. When the parties returned to the written specification, they could identify what had actually been agreed and what required a new decision. The phrase remained useful as an indication of the manager's stance, not as evidence that one interpretation had already been proven. The distinction mattered because a vivid idiom can make an accusation feel established before its basis is examined.",
            sq("What does the idiom establish directly here?", "The manager's perception of a changed expectation", "Conclusive proof of the customer's fault", "The exact contractual scope", "Moved the goalposts tutumu ifade eder; kapsamın kanıtı yazılı specification'dır."),
            sq("What helps resolve the substantive disagreement?", "Reviewing the written specification", "Repeating the idiom more forcefully", "Assuming vivid language proves the accusation", "Actually agreed içeriği, yazılı kapsamla incelenir."),
            "Calling the request 'moving the goalposts' expresses a view; the agreed scope still needs checking.",
            sq("What must not be confused?", "An evaluative idiom with evidence of the agreement", "A written record with all figurative language", "A request with a completed delivery", "Değerlendiren ifade, sözleşme kapsamının yerine geçmez.")),
        s(14, "The committee called the plan economical, while the critic described it as merely cheap. Both referred to the same lower cost, but the words carried different evaluations. Economical suggested efficiency without necessarily sacrificing value; cheap could imply inadequate quality in this context. A later revision used lower-cost when the writer wanted to report the comparison without endorsing either judgement. This did not make the original words interchangeable. It made the difference in stance explicit and allowed the discussion to examine quality separately. Precision depended on recognising not only the shared reference but also the assumptions and attitudes each near-synonym invited the reader to adopt.",
            sq("What differs between the original descriptions?", "Their evaluation of the lower cost", "The price they refer to necessarily", "The number of committees", "Economical verimlilik çağrışımı, cheap bu bağlamda kalite eleştirisi taşıyor."),
            sq("Why choose 'lower-cost' in the revision?", "To report the comparison with less evaluative commitment", "To prove quality is inadequate", "To erase the cost comparison", "Lower-cost, kaliteyi ayrıca incelemeye bırakan daha tarafsız karşılaştırmadır."),
            "One review calls the style 'plain'; another calls it 'unadorned' approvingly.",
            sq("What should a reader consider beyond shared reference?", "The evaluative stance carried by the wording", "Only the number of letters", "A rule that synonyms always have identical tone", "Aynı özelliğe gönderme yapmak, aynı değerlendirme tonu demek değildir.")),
        s(15, "The debate began with an apparent disagreement over whether the intervention worked. On closer inspection, one speaker meant whether it changed behaviour at all, while the other meant whether the benefit justified the resources required. The chair asked them to define the criterion before exchanging further objections. Once they did, both accepted that a small behavioural effect had been observed; their disagreement concerned its practical value. Clarifying the evaluative standard did not settle the policy question, but prevented them from treating acceptance of an effect as automatic endorsement of the intervention. The conversation could then address costs, alternatives and the importance of the measured outcome.",
            sq("What did defining the criterion reveal?", "The speakers were judging different kinds of success.", "Neither speaker accepted any observed effect.", "The policy question had already been settled.", "Works davranış etkisi veya kaynakları haklı çıkarma anlamında farklı kullanılıyordu."),
            sq("What remains disputed?", "The practical value of the observed effect", "Whether either speaker had spoken", "Whether a criterion exists", "Both accepted effect; disagreement concerned practical value ayrımıdır."),
            "An effect exists, but whether it is worth the cost remains contested.",
            sq("Which inference would be unjustified?", "Observed effect automatically proves the policy is worthwhile.", "Cost matters to the evaluation.", "The value judgement is unresolved.", "Etkinin varlığı, maliyet-fayda değerlendirmesini otomatik sonuçlandırmaz.")),
        s(16, "The article opened by describing a neighbourhood as neglected, then quoted only residents who wanted redevelopment. Later paragraphs acknowledged that some residents feared displacement, but presented their concern as a minor obstacle. A critical reader need not assume that the proposed redevelopment was wrong to notice this asymmetry. The opening label and choice of voices guided the reader towards a preferred conclusion before the alternatives were explored. Evaluating the framing therefore involved examining what was emphasised, whose account received authority, and how objections were positioned. This was an analysis of the article's construction, distinct from a complete assessment of the redevelopment policy itself.",
            sq("What constitutes the framing asymmetry?", "Supportive voices and labels receive more authority than objections.", "Every viewpoint receives identical treatment.", "The article contains no evaluative language.", "Neglected etiketi ve supportive voices ön planda; diğer kaygı minor obstacle diye küçültülüyor."),
            sq("What does recognising the framing not require?", "Concluding that the policy itself is necessarily wrong", "Examining the choice of voices", "Noticing the opening label", "Metnin kuruluşunu eleştirmek, politika hakkında tam hüküm vermekle aynı değildir."),
            "The report gives one side extensive quotation and summarises the other as a nuisance.",
            sq("What is a relevant critical observation?", "The presentation distributes authority unequally.", "Both sides necessarily receive equal weight.", "The policy is automatically proven false.", "Alıntı ve nuisance etiketi, sunumda yetki ve ağırlık farkı yaratır.")),
        s(17, "The draft reply stated that the partner's proposal was unrealistic. A senior colleague suggested specifying the constraint instead of attaching a broad judgement to the proposal. The revised reply said the current timetable could not accommodate the additional review without delaying delivery, and offered two alternatives. This was diplomatic without being evasive: it made the obstacle and its consequence clear. The partner could disagree about priorities, but no longer had to defend against an unexplained label. The change preserved the substance of the objection while reducing the personal and evaluative force of the wording, allowing the negotiation to continue around a concrete choice.",
            sq("What makes the revision diplomatic rather than evasive?", "It specifies the constraint and offers alternatives.", "It hides the objection entirely.", "It agrees to every demand silently.", "Constraint, consequence ve alternatives açık olduğu için itiraz kaybolmuyor."),
            sq("What is reduced by removing 'unrealistic'?", "Unexplained evaluative force", "The factual timetable constraint", "Every possible disagreement", "Etiket kaldırılırken somut takvim kısıtı korunur."),
            "We cannot add this review within the present deadline; we could extend the deadline or reduce the scope.",
            sq("What kind of response is this?", "A clear objection with negotiable alternatives", "An unconditional acceptance", "A refusal to explain any constraint", "Kısıt açık, iki seçenek müzakereye açık sunulur.")),
        s(18, "A team discussed fairness as though everyone understood it in the same way. For one member, fairness meant applying identical rules; for another, it meant adjusting support to unequal circumstances. Their examples initially seemed to prove that the other definition was inconsistent. A facilitator asked them to name the principle each example relied on. The discussion became more productive once equality of treatment was distinguished from equity of support. Neither principle answered every case automatically. The team still had to explain when a difference in treatment served a relevant need and when it would become arbitrary preference. Naming the abstract distinction clarified the argument without eliminating the judgement it required.",
            sq("What distinction clarifies the disagreement?", "Identical treatment versus support adjusted to circumstances", "Fairness versus the absence of any rule", "Examples versus all practical decisions as identical", "Eşit işlem ile koşullara göre destek farklı adalet ölçütleridir."),
            sq("Does naming the principles settle every case?", "No, their application still requires judgement.", "Yes, every case becomes automatic.", "No principles remain relevant.", "Neither principle answered every case automatically uygulama yargısının sürdüğünü belirtir."),
            "The same rule may affect people differently; deciding whether to adjust it needs a relevant justification.",
            sq("What must an adjustment demonstrate?", "A relevant reason rather than arbitrary preference", "That rules can never matter", "That every difference is automatically fair", "Relevant justification, farkın gerekçesini şart koşar.")),
        s(19, "The columnist described the institution as a ship taking on water. The metaphor organised several complaints into a picture of imminent danger and implied that decisive intervention was needed. Yet the evidence concerned delays and budget pressures, not necessarily an approaching collapse. A reader could recognise the metaphor's rhetorical force while questioning the degree of urgency it projected. Rewriting the passage in literal terms exposed which claims were supported and which were supplied by the image. This did not make metaphor illegitimate. It made its contribution to the argument visible, including the conclusions the reader might otherwise accept through association rather than through independently presented evidence.",
            sq("What does the metaphor contribute beyond the literal complaints?", "A sense of imminent danger and urgency", "A precise technical measurement of collapse", "A neutral list with no associations", "Taking on water görüntüsü, gecikme ve bütçe baskısından daha büyük tehlike çağrıştırır."),
            sq("Why rewrite the passage literally?", "To distinguish evidenced claims from implications of the image", "To prove all metaphor is forbidden", "To make the evidence inaccessible", "Literal terms, resmin eklediği çıkarımları kanıttan ayırır."),
            "Calling a minor setback a 'catastrophe' adds an evaluation not established by the facts alone.",
            sq("What should the reader examine?", "Whether the evaluative intensity is justified", "Only the word's spelling", "Whether a label automatically proves its own accuracy", "Değerlendirme şiddeti, olgularla orantılı mı diye incelenir.")),
        s(20, "The campaign's message invited the audience to choose between embracing the plan and rejecting progress. A critic argued that this was a false binary: one could support the aim while disputing the proposed means. In a revised version, the speaker acknowledged a plausible alternative and explained why she still preferred her proposal. The argument became less dramatic but more accountable, because its advantage had to be stated relative to a real competitor rather than to an obviously unattractive opposite. Persuasion did not disappear when the binary was removed. It shifted towards a comparison the audience could evaluate, including the cost and uncertainty attached to each option.",
            sq("What makes the original choice a false binary?", "It excludes support for the aim through different means.", "It describes two genuinely exhaustive options.", "It allows every possible alternative equally.", "Amaç desteklenip yöntem tartışılabilir; rejecting progress tek alternatif değildir."),
            sq("What strengthens accountability in the revision?", "Comparison with a plausible alternative", "Comparison only with an absurd opposite", "Removal of every cost and uncertainty", "Gerçek rakip seçenek, üstünlüğün gerekçelendirilmesini gerektirir."),
            "You can agree with the goal while preferring another method.",
            sq("Which claim does this challenge?", "That disagreement with one method means rejection of the goal", "That methods can be compared", "That a goal has been stated", "Amaç ve yöntem ayrımı, ikili karşıtlığın varsayımını bozar."))
    )
}
